<title>LEBANON: Lebanon public debt up 41 pct in 1996 - Banks Assn.</title>
<headline>Lebanon public debt up 41 pct in 1996 - Banks Assn.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's public debt rose by more than 41 percent in 1996, according to figures issued by the Lebanese Banks Association on Monday.</p>
<p>The cumulative deficit of income to expenditure fell to 52 percent from 54 percent at the end of November, the association said. This compared with a target deficit for the year of 37.6 percent, according to the budget law approved by parliament last January.</p>
<p>The association issued the following details of Lebanon's public finances (in billions of Lebanese pounds at end of period unless otherwise stated):</p>
